// std.telemetry T1: the manual tracing surface — `telemetry.span(name)` mints a `Span`, whose
// methods `set_attribute` (chaining, union-typed value) and `end` marshal to the Telemetry Host
// capability. Spans are a write-only side effect (never program output), so this program's OWN
// output is what the differential pins; that both backends type-check and run the module function
// + the extern-type methods identically is the end-to-end proof. (The recorded spans themselves are
// asserted in the noeta-stdlib unit test, against the sandbox recorder.)
// expect: stdout "start"
// expect: stdout "done"
// expect: exit 0
use std.{telemetry}

echo "start"

// A span with two attributes (string + int through the value union), chained then ended.
s = telemetry.span("request").set_attribute("http.method", "GET").set_attribute("http.status", 200)
s.end()

// A second, independent span with a bool attribute; the whole chain ends in `end()` (unit).
telemetry.span("work").set_attribute("cache.hit", true).end()

echo "done"
